  "worked_solution": "The set $S$ contains all natural numbers greater than or equal to $5.$\n\nTherefore, the set can be written as\n\n$$\nS={x\\in N\\,:\\,x\\ge 5}.\n$$\n\n**Note**: This definition is not unique. For example:\n\n- We can write $x\\in Z.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS={x\\in Z\\,:x\\ge 5}.\n$$\n\n- We can write $x>4.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS={x\\in N\\,:\\,x>4},\n$$\n\nor, writing $x\\in Z$ as before, we have\n\n$$\nS={x\\in Z\\,:\\,x>4}.\n$$",
